<section id="concepts" class="band">
    <span class="kicker">Four concepts</span>
    <h2 class="chrome reveal">The engine is how, an identity is who, a pack is what.</h2>
    <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="panel reveal">
            <h3>The engine is how</h3>
            <p>The loop, streaming, the guards, the ledger and handing work to other sessions. It names no product; every host is a library a few lines of yours start. <a href="/architecture">The whole map</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="panel reveal" data-delay="1">
            <h3>An identity is who</h3>
            <p>Its voice, its roles and the packs it names, as markdown in a project of its own. Puls, the coding agent and the guide in this page's corner are identities. <a href="/identities">Identities</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="panel reveal" data-delay="2">
            <h3>A pack is what</h3>
            <p>Tools and their guide, as a package that needs only the contracts. Written once, used by any identity, and served over MCP as it is. <a href="/packs">Every pack</a></p>
        </article>
    </div>
    <p class="band-note">The fourth, a workflow, is how one agent delegates to another and decides on what comes back. It is planned, and the engine's job: <a href="/whats-coming">what's coming</a>.</p>
</section>

